    // Time 8-13: att1 serves row 2, att2 serves row 4
    // Time 14: both move forward 1 row
    // Time 15-20: att1 serves row 5, att2 serves row 7
    // Time 21: both move forward 1 row
    // Time 22-27: att1 serves row 6, att2 serves row 8
    // Time 28: both move forward 1 row
    // ...

    // So for row n, we need to figure out which "step" it is in.
    // Attendant 1 serves rows: 1, 2, 5, 6, 9, 10, ...
    // Attendant 2 serves rows: 3, 4, 7, 8, 11, 12, ...

    // For attendant 1, the rows are: 1, 2, 5, 6, 9, 10, ...
